### =====================================================================
### product-service - ready-to-run requests (WRITE side of the catalog)
###
### Calls the service DIRECTLY on port 8104, so we send the X-User-* and X-Store-Id
### headers ourselves (normally the API gateway adds them from the JWT).
### Written for the VS Code "REST Client" extension: run the requests in order
### (request 4 names the new product; later requests reuse its id).
###
### Reading products (lists, search) is NOT here: GET requests go to product-read-service,
### see product-read-service/http/product-read-service.http.
###
### Seed data: store 1 = Fresh Mart (vendor user 3), store 2 = Green Basket (vendor user 6),
### categories 1 Vegetables, 2 Fruits, 3 Dairy & Eggs, 4 Snacks & Beverages, 5 Household.
### =====================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8104
@productId = {{createProduct.response.body.$.data.id}}
@categoryId = {{createCategory.response.body.$.data.id}}


### 1. ADMIN: create a category (run once; a second run gives 409)
# @name createCategory
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/categories
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 2
X-User-Role: ADMIN

{
  "name": "Bakery & Bread",
  "description": "Fresh bread, buns and cakes",
  "displayOrder": 6
}


### 2. ADMIN: rename the category (products in it get the new name in search, via Debezium)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/categories/{{categoryId}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 2
X-User-Role: ADMIN

{
  "name": "Bakery",
  "description": "Fresh bread, buns and cakes",
  "displayOrder": 6
}


### 3. ADMIN: a category name that already exists -> 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/categories
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 2
X-User-Role: ADMIN

{
  "name": "Vegetables"
}


### 4. VENDOR (store 1): add a product -> sellingPrice is calculated (45.00 - 10 % = 40.50)
# @name createProduct
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/products
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 3
X-User-Role: VENDOR
X-Store-Id: 1

{
  "categoryId": 1,
  "name": "Cherry Tomato",
  "description": "Sweet cherry tomatoes, great for salads",
  "brand": "Fresho",
  "sku": "FM-VEG-020",
  "unit": "G",
  "unitQuantity": 250,
  "price": 45.00,
  "discountPercentage": 10,
  "taxPercentage": 0
}


### 5. VENDOR (store 1): change the price -> 50.00 - 20 % = 40.00
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/products/{{productId}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 3
X-User-Role: VENDOR
X-Store-Id: 1

{
  "categoryId": 1,
  "name": "Cherry Tomato",
  "description": "Sweet cherry tomatoes, great for salads",
  "brand": "Fresho",
  "sku": "FM-VEG-020",
  "unit": "G",
  "unitQuantity": 250,
  "price": 50.00,
  "discountPercentage": 20,
  "taxPercentage": 0
}


### 6. VENDOR (store 1): upload a product image (JPEG, PNG or WEBP, max 2 MB)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/products/{{productId}}/images
X-User-Id: 3
X-User-Role: VENDOR
X-Store-Id: 1
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=GroceryBoundary

--GroceryBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="image"; filename="sample-product.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./sample-product.png
--GroceryBoundary--


### 7. VENDOR (store 1): hide the product (INACTIVE)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/products/{{productId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 3
X-User-Role: VENDOR
X-Store-Id: 1

{
  "status": "INACTIVE"
}


### 8. VENDOR (store 1): show it again (ACTIVE)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/products/{{productId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 3
X-User-Role: VENDOR
X-Store-Id: 1

{
  "status": "ACTIVE"
}


### 9. VENDOR (store 2): another store's product -> 404 (multi-tenant rule)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/products/{{productId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 6
X-User-Role: VENDOR
X-Store-Id: 2

{
  "status": "INACTIVE"
}


### 10. VENDOR without an approved store (no X-Store-Id) -> 403
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/products
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 10
X-User-Role: VENDOR

{
  "categoryId": 1,
  "name": "Test",
  "sku": "T-1",
  "unit": "KG",
  "unitQuantity": 1,
  "price": 10,
  "taxPercentage": 0
}


### 11. VENDOR: invalid product -> 400 with one error per field
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/products
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 3
X-User-Role: VENDOR
X-Store-Id: 1

{
  "categoryId": 1,
  "name": "",
  "sku": "bad sku!",
  "unit": "G",
  "unitQuantity": 0,
  "price": 0,
  "discountPercentage": 95,
  "taxPercentage": 0
}


### 12. ADMIN: block the product (moderation) -> hidden from customers
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/products/{{productId}}/block
X-User-Id: 2
X-User-Role: ADMIN


### 13. VENDOR (store 1): cannot activate a blocked product -> 400
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/products/{{productId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 3
X-User-Role: VENDOR
X-Store-Id: 1

{
  "status": "ACTIVE"
}


### 14. ADMIN: unblock it -> ACTIVE again
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/products/{{productId}}/unblock
X-User-Id: 2
X-User-Role: ADMIN


### 15. VENDOR (store 1): delete the product (soft delete; it disappears from search)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/products/{{productId}}
X-User-Id: 3
X-User-Role: VENDOR
X-Store-Id: 1


### =====================================================================
### Reviews (Phase 11). A customer reviews a product of one of their DELIVERED orders; product-service asks
### order-service (needs it running). Seed: customer1's order 1 contains Tomato (product 1) once it is delivered,
### e.g. after e2e/phase7-order-saga.http. Put a delivered order of customer1 in @deliveredOrderId.
### =====================================================================

@deliveredOrderId = 1


### 16. CUSTOMER (user 4): review the tomatoes of a delivered order (4 stars)
# @name review
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products/1/reviews
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 4
X-User-Role: CUSTOMER

{
  "orderId": {{deliveredOrderId}},
  "rating": 4,
  "comment": "Fresh and firm"
}


### 17. CUSTOMER (user 4): the same product of the same order again -> 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products/1/reviews
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 4
X-User-Role: CUSTOMER

{
  "orderId": {{deliveredOrderId}},
  "rating": 5
}


### 18. CUSTOMER (user 7): someone else's order -> 404
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products/1/reviews
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 7
X-User-Role: CUSTOMER

{
  "orderId": {{deliveredOrderId}},
  "rating": 1
}


### 19. CUSTOMER: 6 stars -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products/1/reviews
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 4
X-User-Role: CUSTOMER

{
  "orderId": {{deliveredOrderId}},
  "rating": 6
}


### 20. PUBLIC: the visible reviews of Tomato, newest first
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products/1/reviews


### 21. VENDOR (store 1): reviews of my products, e.g. only 1-star ones
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/reviews?rating=1
X-User-Id: 3
X-User-Role: VENDOR
X-Store-Id: 1


### 22. ADMIN: all reviews of Tomato
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/reviews?productId=1
X-User-Id: 2
X-User-Role: ADMIN


### 23. ADMIN: hide the review (the product's rating is recalculated without it)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/reviews/{{review.response.body.$.data.id}}/hide
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: 2
X-User-Role: ADMIN

{
  "reason": "Not about the product"
}


### 24. ADMIN: show it again
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/reviews/{{review.response.body.$.data.id}}/show
X-User-Id: 2
X-User-Role: ADMIN
